# Accepted Trivy findings, with the reason each is accepted.
#
# Anything listed here must carry a justification a reviewer can check. An
# undocumented suppression is indistinguishable from a missed finding, and the
# point of the scan is to be believed.

# DS-0002 — "Specify at least 1 USER command in Dockerfile with non-root user"
#
# False positive for this image. The Dockerfile genuinely has no USER directive,
# because privilege is dropped at runtime rather than at build time:
# backend/entrypoint.sh validates PUID/PGID, refuses 0 explicitly, creates the
# user and group, chowns /app/uploads, then execs the app through
# `gosu "$APP_UID:$APP_GID"`. The container starts as root only long enough to
# set that up, and the process always ends up unprivileged (UID/GID 1000 by
# default).
#
# The PUID/PGID contract is deliberate — it is what lets a self-hoster line the
# container's ownership up with their own volume permissions, which a build-time
# USER cannot do. A static check cannot see any of that, so it reports the
# absence of the directive rather than the presence of the drop.
#
# Re-examine if entrypoint.sh stops dropping privilege.
DS-0002
